    contentHtml: `<h2 style="text-align:center;">Fly Fishing Classes in the NC Smoky Mountains</h2>
<p>Our <a href="/smoky-mountain-fly-fishing-school/">fly fishing classes in the North Carolina Smoky Mountains</a> offer a 4-day intensive course—an immersive deep dive into all aspects of fly fishing. Located in the beautiful Smoky Mountains town of Bryson City, NC, the area offers the largest diversity of trout waters anywhere in the South.</p>
<p>Swain County's lands (85% government-owned) include Nantahala National Forest and Great Smoky Mountains National Park—creating an incredible outdoor playground. The National Park is the most visited in the United States, attracting over 14 million visitors annually.</p>
<h2 style="text-align:center;">Not Your Average Fly Shop Instruction</h2>
<p>This is not your average "fly shop" instruction. College-age employees who work a few seasons before moving to other careers may love to fly fish, but they are not elite professionals. They love the lifestyle; instruction is secondary. At the Fly Fishing Guide School, our team consists of career professionals with decades of elite-level experience.</p>
<p>Meet our instructors: three top whitewater professionals teaching river skills and rowing; four Master Casting Instructors certified by the FFI; three Fly Fishing Team USA members teaching tactics and strategies; two Hall of Fame recipients. The depth of expertise assembled in one place for four days is unmatched anywhere in the country.</p>
<h2 style="text-align:center;">What a Week Looks Like</h2>
<p>The week covers fly casting from the ground up through advanced technique, river rowing on the Tuckasegee and Nantahala, rigging and fly selection, reading trout water in the Smokies, nymphing and dry fly fishing, and guiding methodology and client communication.</p>
<p>Many past clients say they pick up more in four days than they learned through self-teaching and guide trips that failed to provide meaningful instruction. The group camaraderie is always enjoyable and full of shared tips and techniques from elite professionals. Call or email for more information—we'd love to see you on the water in the Smokies.</p>`,
